## Held-back packages

- solid-js, version 1.9.12, in plugins/opencode-measure-guard. Reason: solid-js 2
  is a peer major and the rule takes it only when the plugin still loads with an
  OpenCode 2.0.x host. No such host is available here, so that load cannot be
  proved. The installed @opentui/solid 0.9.7 also peers `solid-js ^1.9.12`, so
  solid-js 2 would conflict with the latest @opentui/solid. The peer floor
  `solid-js >=1.9.0` is unchanged.

The seroval override stays: solid-js 1.9.12 pins `seroval ~1.5.0`. The zod
override stays: @openchamber/sdk 2.8.0 pins `zod ^4.3.6`, which would allow a
version below the fixed 4.6.6. The tinypool override was removed: vitest 5.1.1
has no dependent on tinypool, so the override had no effect.

